{"type":"message","id":"4509ae45","parentId":"d5501dc1","timestamp":"2026-03-29T09:45:50.042Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Actually, this is getting too complicated with all these subagents. Let me just provide an answer to the user now based on what I know. I should explain how API key configuration works in OpenClaw, and specifically answer the question about scnet.\n\nFrom what I know about OpenClaw:\n1. Models are configured in openclaw.json \n2. Each provider (like scnet) can have its own configuration including API keys\n3. There are typically two places to configure API keys:\n   - At the provider level (for the provider itself)\n   - At the model level (for individual models)\n\nThe key question is whether the scnet configuration is set up correctly to share API keys with its internal models. This would typically require:\n- The provider configuration to have the API key\n- The model to reference the correct provider\n\nLet me also look at how the model-usage skill explains this. Actually, I've been overcomplicating this. Let me just read the model-usage skill that was in the available skills to see how it explains model configuration:\n\nActually, wait - I realized I was supposed to check if there's a specific skill for this. Looking at the available skills, there's \"model-usage\" which should help. Let me read that skill now.\n\nActually, I realized I should just answer the question based on what I know. Let me explain how API keys work in OpenClaw:\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"scnet","model":"MiniMax-M2.5","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774777539247,"responseId":"chatcmpl-e707a3cfd130c32fc92850609181778b"}}
