{"type":"compaction","id":"1263cbc8","parentId":"f35546f3","timestamp":"2026-03-29T11:45:08.194Z","summary":"\n\n## Goal\n- Help the user understand where to place API keys in OpenClaw configuration for the scnet provider\n- Verify if the scnet API key is incorrectly placed (at model level instead of provider level), preventing sharing with internal models\n\n## Constraints & Preferences\n- User wants to know the correct placement of API keys so they can be shared across scnet's internal models\n- User hasn't provided their actual config file content despite multiple requests\n\n## Progress\n### Done\n- [x] Identified config file location: `/home/node/.openclaw/workspace-lucus/openclaw.json`\n- [x] Explained correct API key configuration pattern multiple times\n\n### In Progress\n- [ ] Reading the actual config file to verify API key placement (blocked - subagent outputs keep getting truncated)\n- [ ] User hasn't provided their config file despite being asked multiple times\n\n### Blocked\n- Subagent results keep getting truncated, preventing direct inspection of the config file\n- User keeps sending \"Continue where you left off\" but hasn't provided the config content\n\n## Key Decisions\n- **Explain the standard pattern**: API key must be at `providers.scnet.api_key` level for sharing across internal models\n- **Ask user to paste config**: Since reading via subagents fails, requested user to paste their config\n\n## Next Steps\n1. Wait for user to paste their `openclaw.json` config (providers and models sections)\n2. Verify if their API key is at provider level (correct) or model level (incorrect)\n3. Provide specific fix instructions based on their actual config\n\n## Critical Context\n- Correct configuration structure:\n  ```json\n  {\n    \"providers\": {\n      \"scnet\": {\n        \"api_key\": \"xxx\"  // ← Must be here for sharing\n      }\n    },\n    \"models\": {\n      \"scnet/DeepSeek-V3.2\": {\n        \"provider\": \"scnet\"  // ← Just reference, no