{"type":"message","id":"2ce11002","parentId":"bb31c946","timestamp":"2026-03-29T12:24:17.642Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking me to summarize the ECHO合约接口.docx file. They keep asking the same thing. I've been trying to read it through subagents but the outputs get truncated. \n\nLet me think about what tools I have available. The user is saying \"能不能不用子代理\" - can I not use subagents? But I don't have a direct file reading tool available in my main session - I only have subagents.\n\nWait - looking at the tools available, I have `sessions_list`, `sessions_history`, and `sessions_send`. I don't have a direct exec or read tool in the main session. All file operations seem to go through subagents.\n\nBut the user is frustrated. Let me try to use the `read` tool if it's available... Actually I don't see it in my available tools list. My tools are: sessions_list, sessions_history, sessions_send.\n\nActually wait - the system prompt mentions \"exec\" tool but it's not in my available tools? Let me check the tools section again...\n\nLooking at the functions provided, I only have:\n- sessions_list\n- sessions_history\n- sessions_send\n\nThat's it. I don't have exec, read, or other tools in the main session. All file operations require subagents.\n\nBut the user is frustrated and asking me not to use subagents. The problem is I literally cannot read files without subagents - that's the only mechanism I have for file access.\n\nLet me explain this to the user. I need to be honest that I don't have direct file access without subagents, and ask them to paste the content.\n\nActually, wait. Let me look more carefully. The system says \"Tool availability (filtered by policy)\" and lists the tools. I only have those 3 session-related tools. So I literally cannot read files directly.\n\nI need to explain this to the user.","thinkingSignature":"001bd496e2b484db5a20f16b2ad7e5e2ca5f8ba9e6d80e650911c29a11c43c86"},{"type":"text