{"type":"message","id":"eb70c01f","parentId":"5946ee2f","timestamp":"2026-03-29T12:38:56.478Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking me to continue. But I keep getting the same results - subagent outputs are truncated. I've been asking the user to paste the content directly, but they're not doing that. Instead they keep asking me to try again.\n\nLet me think about what I can do differently. The subagent ran successfully (39 seconds) but the output is truncated. The issue is that the subagent's full output doesn't get returned to me - I only see a summary in the session list.\n\nActually, wait. Looking at the sessions_list results, I can see:\n- status: \"done\"\n- runtimeMs: 39359 (39 seconds - so it ran the python script)\n- totalTokens: 11300\n\nThe subagent ran and generated tokens, so it must have produced output. But I can't see the actual text content because the output is truncated in the notification I receive.\n\nThe user is frustrated because I keep asking them to paste the content. But they keep asking me to try again. \n\nMaybe I should try a different approach. Instead of running a subagent that prints the text, maybe I should ask the subagent to write the text to a file in the workspace, and then I can read that file? But wait, I don't have a read tool in my main session...\n\nActually, there's another option. The subagent could write the content to a file in the workspace directory, and then I could use sessions_send to send a message to another session to read that file? No, that doesn't make sense.\n\nLet me think about this more carefully. The subagent ran python-docx and extracted text from the docx file. The text was printed to stdout. But the output gets truncated when it's returned to me.\n\nOne approach: Instead of printing the full text, the subagent could write the text to a file, and then I could use a different tool to read just the beginning of that file? But I don't have a read tool...\n\nWait, actually - the subagent is a sessions_spawn. When it completes, its output is supposed to be returned to me. But it seems like the output is being truncated. \n\nI'm hitting the same wall with each attempt. The core problem is that my subagent produces content but the notification system truncates what I can see, and I lack the tools to access the full output directly. The user keeps expecting me to find a way through, but I've exhausted the obvious approaches given my current constraints.","thinkingSignature":"7b83fe0fc232c7cf8d3147e1a0d17f02b273213ed0818b3f2f5b43c27bcffc1b"},{"type":"text","text":"[[reply_to_current]] 我试了很多次了，每次子代理输出都被截断，我看不到文档内容。\n\n这不是能力问题，是系统设计限制：**子代理的完整输出不会返回给我**。\n\n**唯一解决办法：你把文档内容复制贴过来，我立刻总结。**"}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"minimax-m2.5:free","usage":{"input":38,"output":559,"cacheRead":3281,"cacheWrite":130650,"totalTokens":134528,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1774787911883,"responseId":"061850487794587f795bddfec6f6641c"}}
