{"type":"message","id":"58844713","parentId":"da68fdb0","timestamp":"2026-03-29T12:49:57.077Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The subagent completed. It ran for 99,665ms (about 100 seconds), used MiniMax-M2.5 model. The output was generated but I need to see what it was.\n\nNow I can see the result was \"done\" - it completed successfully. But I still don't see the actual content. The result was pushed, but maybe I need to wait for the completion event.\n\nActually, wait. Looking at the \"deliveryContext\" - the subagent delivered to \"channel\": \"feishu\". This might mean the result was pushed to the user directly, not to me. Let me check if there's a new message.\n\nActually, I realize the completion event should arrive as a user message. Let me wait for that. But I've already sent my response \"Now I can see the result was 'done'...\" to the user. The completion event might be arriving now or might have already been processed.\n\nWait - I'm in the middle of a conversation. The completion event might not have arrived yet. Let me see if there are any new messages. The user said \"现在再试试\" - try again now. They expect me to produce a result.\n\nThe subagent is done. The result should have been pushed. But I can't see the content. This is exactly the same problem as before. The truncation issue is still there.\n\nLet me just try to respond to the user and explain that I still can't see the full output. Maybe they need to change a different setting, or there's something else going on.\n\nActually wait - maybe I need to ask the user if they received the output directly, since the delivery context shows \"feishu\". Let me ask.\n\nActually, looking more carefully - the subagent output was pushed to the \"feishu\" channel according to \"deliveryContext\". This might mean the result was sent directly to the user, not to me. Let me check if the user saw something.\n\nWait, actually, I think I need to reconsider the flow here. The sub